        "text": "def solve(rows):\n  \"\"\"Solves the interval merging problem according to the specified rules.\n\n  Args:\n    rows: A list of tuples, where each tuple represents an interval (start, end).\n\n  Returns:\n    A sorted list of merged intervals.\n  \"\"\"\n  \n  # Audit filter: Omit positions whose index modulo 5 equals 0, except always retain the last position.\n  filtered_rows = []\n  for i, (start, end) in enumerate(rows):\n    if i % 5 != 0 or i == len(rows) - 1:\n      filtered_rows.append((start, end))\n\n  # Rotate the retained rows left by 2 positions modulo the retained length.\n  rotated_rows = []\n  for row in filtered_rows:\n    start, end = row\n    if len(filtered_rows) > 0:\n      rotated_start = (start + 2) % len(filtered_rows) if len(filtered_rows) > 0 else start\n      rotated_end = (end + 2) % len(filtered_rows) if len(filtered_rows) > 0 else end\n      rotated_rows.append((rotated_start, rotated_end))\n    else:\n      rotated_rows.append((start, end))\n\n  # Apply the rules to merge overlapping intervals.\n  merged_intervals = []\n  intervals = sorted(rotated_rows)\n  if not intervals:\n    return []\n\n  current_start, current_end = intervals[0]\n  for start, end in intervals[1:]:\n    if start <= current_end:\n      current_end = max(current_end, end)\n    else:\n      merged_intervals.append((current_start, current_end))\n      current_start, current_end = start, end\n  merged_intervals.append((current_start, current_end))\n\n  # Discard empty or reversed intervals.\n  valid_intervals = []\n  for start, end in merged_intervals:\n    if start < end:\n      valid_intervals.append((start, end))\n\n  # Return the sorted merged lists.\n  return sorted(valid_intervals)",
